    {
      "id": "focus",
      "type": "cv.focus_stack",
      "name": "Focus stack images",
      "documentation": "<p>Fuse registered captures using local luminance focus energy. Align images upstream with registration/warp blocks, supplying coverage masks for resampling gaps. Focus indices are original zero-based batch indices, with -1 where no reliable fusion occurs. Exact ties prefer the anchor, then batch order. Flat/ambiguous pixels retain the anchor; they do not silently acquire an invented focus level.</p><p>Unsigned images share integer full scale; floating images share one batch peak. Scores use this scale, not independent per-frame normalization. Strict support erodes coverage by the prefilter/derivative/window halo. Alpha is excluded from scoring and retained from the anchor; transparent samples cannot supply neighborhoods. Weighted fusion may soften detail, while hard fusion retains original pixel values. Focus level/confidence are diagnostics, not surface depth or visibility proof.</p><p><a href=\"https://docs.opencv.org/5.0/main_modules/imgproc_filter.html\">OpenCV filter reference</a>.</p>",
      "parameters": {
        "anchor_index": 0,
        "alignment": "pixel_grid",
        "method": "tenengrad",
        "aperture": "3",
        "window": 9,
        "prefilter": "off",
        "prefilter_sigma": 0.0,
        "border": "reflect_101",
        "support": "strict",
        "minimum_contributors": 2,
        "minimum_energy": 1e-06,
        "minimum_confidence": 0.05,
        "minimum_valid_fraction": 0.3,
        "blend": "hard",
        "blend_power": 2.0,
        "weight_radius": 0
      },
      "position": [
        700.0,
        100.0
      ],
      "node_size": "large",
      "exposed_inputs": [
        "images",
        "coverage",
        "mask",
        "region"
      ],
      "exposed_outputs": [
        "image",
        "focus_index",
        "valid_mask",
        "info"
      ],
      "thumbnail": true,
      "preview_output": ""
    },
